  ],
  "preconditions": [
    "Owned local Linux project; exact independent publication request and native writer lock.",
    "Released original writer lock; current transaction-bound recovery lock and explicit host authority for terminal cleanup.",
    "Explicit transaction-bound host authority; real stopped Linux processes and native root mutex for orphan recovery; independent normative byte oracle.",
    "Recovery derivative publication requires native Linux O_TMPFILE support and a usable /proc/self/fd link; unsupported operations fail without a named-write fallback."
  ],
  "steps": [
    "Publish verified target files using the existing transaction phases.",
    "Create bound receipts, synchronize them and only then persist committed.",
    "Assert normative inputs are not written again and failed completion retains evidence.",
    "Restore a partially published transaction and verify its canonical immutable rollback receipt; verify the canonical discard receipt separately.",
    "In independent processes complete or roll back, verify terminal evidence, explicitly archive the closed work inventory, then permit a normal reader and new writer.",
    "Retry without normative writes; reject changed evidence, live bytes, unsafe images and unknown work while retaining unrelated active blockers.",
    "Inject receipt, marker, intent, archive and barrier failures; repeat the selected terminal action and cleanup without replacing immutable evidence or rewriting normative files.",
    "Repeat an interrupted terminal discard using the independent preflight and original event binding; preserve short or conflicting receipts.",
    "Abruptly stop writer and recovery processes; explicitly acquire audited transaction recovery access, then verify completion and retained foreign blockers.",
    "Interrupt the remaining nine bound recovery derivative writes, repeat native interruptions and abruptly stop processes; resume with audited native lock takeover, retain original images and prove independent basis/full-target bytes without a second normative replacement.",
    "Reject foreign empty/short/conflicting or unsafe files and concurrent prefix collisions; recheck journal, lock, live normative bytes and prior evidence before publication. Reuse complete records without changing their authority attribution; finish existing preserving cleanup.",
    "In fresh writer/recovery processes, reconstruct explicit building/prepared discard inputs and retain the original immutable audit and receipt through selected interrupted completion boundaries; compare independent basis bytes, repeated results and next-writer access."
  ],
  "oracle": {
    "kind": "behavior",
    "requirement_contract": "Eine erfolgreich abgeschlossene oder zurückgerollte Transaktion MUSS einen unveränderbaren Abschlussbeleg unter `.specroad/transactions/receipts/` hinterlassen und danach das Entfernen temporärer Payloads erlauben.",
    "scope": "Native committed finalization/readback, immutable rolled-back/discarded receipts and explicit recovery-lock cleanup after writer release or audited orphan takeover. Lost terminal evidence, rename and synchronization responses preserve exact bytes; a bound pending marker keeps interrupted archival active. Bound rollback copies, cursor/terminal journals, completion receipts/marker and action/rollback receipts are published only after complete staging. Initial allocation/write failures expose no short canonical helper. Tested repeated native failures and real process stops remain explicitly resumable; foreign or altered bindings block publication, existing evidence retains its bytes and original authority, and mutation diagnostics retain possible operational changes. Selected persisted-input discard restart cases retain the original audit/receipt and complete basis without normative writes; interrupted completion resumes in a fresh process and preserves conflicting evidence. No whole CLI, restore or complete failure/restart acceptance."
  },
